# Decode worker argument set (TP=2 on GPU 2-3). Carries the DSpark
# speculative configuration: the draft state relay across the PD boundary is
# consumed on the decode side, so the DSPARK flags live here and only here.
# Consumed by deploy/launch/serve.sh; one flag per line, blank lines
# and # comments ignored. File paths are resolved relative to the repo root.
--model-path deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731
--served-model-name deepseek-v4-flash-dspark
--tp 2
--trust-remote-code
--disaggregation-mode decode
--disaggregation-transfer-backend mooncake
--speculative-algorithm DSPARK
# gamma=5 is the checkpoint's native dspark_block_size; SGLang infers it from
# the checkpoint when the flag is unset, and it is pinned here for explicitness.
--speculative-dspark-block-size 5
# SPS step-cost table: required by this deployment's launch gate (without it
# SGLang falls back to an uninitialized flat table and the budget planner
# degenerates to verify-all). Generated on this host via `make calibrate`
# (scripts/calibrate_sps_sts.sh).
--speculative-dspark-sps-table-path configs/dspark_sps_table.json
# STS confidence calibration: optional. The launch script drops this flag when
# the table does not exist, so the engine runs without STS tuning.
--speculative-dspark-confidence-sts-path configs/dspark_sts_table.json
--speculative-moe-runner-backend flashinfer_mxfp4
--moe-runner-backend flashinfer_mxfp4
--swa-full-tokens-ratio 0.1
# Lower pool fraction than the prefill side: the decode pool carries the
# resident weights plus the bundled drafter and its CUDA-graph buffers.
--mem-fraction-static 0.93
--max-running-requests 32
--cuda-graph-max-bs-decode 32
--enable-metrics
